  "notes": "{諌|いさ}める is a transitive ichidan verb. Also written as {諫|いさ}める.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{諌|いさ}めている indicates the act of admonishing is ongoing.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- を{諌|いさ}める (to admonish someone)\n- に{諌|いさ}められる (to be admonished by)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {主君|しゅくん}を{諌|いさ}める (to remonstrate with one's lord)\n- {暴走|ぼうそう}を{諌|いさ}める (to counsel against recklessness)\n\nThis word has a literary and formal tone. It implies advising against something wrong or dangerous, typically from a lower-status person to a higher-status one. In modern usage, it appears in news and formal writing more than casual speech.",
